From: dianqk <jufaye2014@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pipeline: simple: Do not trust cached link flags

MediaLink flags are read when the media graph is enumerated and are only
updated by the current process. When another process (for example cam
while PipeWire holds the camera manager) routes a different sensor to a
shared receiver, the cached flags of that link still read disabled.
setupLinks() then skips disabling it and enabling the new link fails with
-EBUSY on receivers that accept a single source, such as the Qualcomm
CAMSS CSID.

Disable every mutable link on the pipeline pads and enable the pipeline
link without consulting the cache. The media core returns early for
requests that do not change the link state, so this costs one ioctl per
link.

---
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -795,8 +795,15 @@
 				if (link == sinkLink)
 					continue;
 
-				if ((link->flags() & MEDIA_LNK_FL_ENABLED) &&
-				    !(link->flags() & MEDIA_LNK_FL_IMMUTABLE)) {
+				/*
+				 * The cached link flags are only updated by this
+				 * process. Another process may have enabled a link
+				 * since the media graph was enumerated, so disable
+				 * every mutable link instead of trusting the cache.
+				 * The kernel ignores requests that do not change the
+				 * link state.
+				 */
+				if (!(link->flags() & MEDIA_LNK_FL_IMMUTABLE)) {
 					ret = link->setEnabled(false);
 					if (ret < 0)
 						return ret;
@@ -804,11 +811,9 @@
 			}
 		}
 
-		if (!(sinkLink->flags() & MEDIA_LNK_FL_ENABLED)) {
-			ret = sinkLink->setEnabled(true);
-			if (ret < 0)
-				return ret;
-		}
+		ret = sinkLink->setEnabled(true);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return ret;
 
 		sinkLink = e.sourceLink;
 	}
